1
00:00:00,030 --> 00:00:01,690
Hello, math explorers!

2
00:00:01,970 --> 00:00:04,090
Today we're solving
seven plus five.

3
00:00:04,390 --> 00:00:05,110
Are you ready?

4
00:00:05,772 --> 00:00:08,412
First, we have seven
delicious red apples.

5
00:00:08,702 --> 00:00:09,572
Let's count them!

6
00:00:09,962 --> 00:00:12,975
One, two, three, four,
five, six, seven.

7
00:00:13,727 --> 00:00:15,837
Now, let's add five more apples.

8
00:00:16,227 --> 00:00:17,497
Here come the green ones!

9
00:00:17,907 --> 00:00:20,287
One, two, three, four, five.

10
00:00:20,497 --> 00:00:22,417
How many apples do
we have altogether?

11
00:00:23,098 --> 00:00:25,218
Seven needs three
more to make ten.

12
00:00:25,428 --> 00:00:27,218
We take three from
our five apples.

13
00:00:27,648 --> 00:00:29,948
Now we have ten,
with two left over.

14
00:00:30,428 --> 00:00:32,368
Ten plus two equals twelve!

15
00:00:33,119 --> 00:00:33,936
Great job!

16
00:00:34,209 --> 00:00:36,189
Seven plus five equals twelve!

17
00:00:36,519 --> 00:00:38,009
Look at all twelve apples.

18
00:00:38,780 --> 00:00:40,330
Let's remember how we did it.

19
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:42,693
Seven plus five is the same

20
00:00:42,768 --> 00:00:44,540
as seven plus three plus two.

21
00:00:45,190 --> 00:00:46,991
Seven plus three is ten,

22
00:00:47,080 --> 00:00:48,930
and ten plus two is twelve.

23
00:00:49,420 --> 00:00:51,217
Remember, making ten helps

24
00:00:51,245 --> 00:00:53,080
us add numbers more easily!
